  "id": "COMPOUND:19464 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Dorsmanin D is shown to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to SNB-78 through a series of biochemical pathways. The first pathway involves Dorsmanin D directly targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is then targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. This compound is further shown to target SNB-78, suggesting a direct interaction between Dorsmanin D and SNB-78 via this chain of targets. The second pathway involves Dorsmanin D targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is also targeted by the same epoxy compound, reinforcing the role of this intermediate in the pathway. A third pathway links Dorsmanin D to Erysimoside, which in turn targets SNB-78, adding another layer of evidence for the relationship. These findings collectively suggest that Dorsmanin D exerts its effects on SNB-78 through a complex network of molecular interactions, with the epoxy compound acting as a central mediator. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Dorsmanin D and SNB-78, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
